Do not make every interaction equally long. Repeated survival tasks should be tactile but efficient, while rare or dangerous tasks can demand more deliberate input.
1.2 A Train That Is a Genuine Moving Base
The train is not merely a vehicle with a decorative interior. It is a modular, persistent construction that travels through the world.
Players should be able to:
	•	Attach and detach train cars.
	•	Install engines, storage, workshops, sleeping areas, kitchens, defensive platforms, generators, and special modules.
	•	Physically transport collected resources and machinery.
	•	Customize interior layouts and exterior armor.
	•	Repair individual parts of the train.
	•	Expand their storage and production capacity at the cost of added mass, power consumption, or maintenance.
	•	Lose individual modules to damage if protection fails.
Core trade-off: More train capacity improves long-term survival, but a larger train costs more fuel, requires more maintenance, and is harder to defend during The Pursuit.
