3. World Architecture and Infinite Railway
3.1 World Coordinates and Streaming
Generate the railway as a sequence of contiguous world chunks.
Each chunk owns:
	•	Track spline sections.
	•	Terrain and landscape meshes.
	•	Biome parameters.
	•	Resource nodes.
	•	Structure placement candidates.
	•	Local ambient audio settings.
	•	Environmental effects.
	•	Navigation data for spawned structures.
	•	A deterministic generation seed.
	•	Persistent object identifiers for stateful world objects.
Use a local coordinate frame around the train and stream distant chunks in and out. This avoids accumulating large floating-point coordinate errors during long-distance travel.
