The durations in the table provide a 45-minute reference cycle when added together. For implementation, choose a single consistent cycle configuration and use it everywhere.
Recommended final clock: 30 minutes of day, consisting of 3 minutes of dawn transition, 24 minutes of full day, and 3 minutes of dusk transition, followed by 18 minutes of night. The full cycle is 48 real minutes.
For the 18-minute night, use these internal phases:
	•	0–3 minutes: Nightfall.
	•	3–12 minutes: Deep night.
	•	12–15 minutes: Predawn tension.
	•	15–18 minutes: Dawn transition.
Use these four internal phases without changing the overall night duration. The nighttime phase names are not additional time added to the cycle.
Lighting implementation
Use a physically plausible directional light, environment lighting, fog, and localized artificial lights.
	•	Day: Broad environmental fill, warmer sun at low angles, stronger visibility, and visible distant landscape landmarks.
	•	Dusk: Reduce directional intensity progressively; allow the sky to retain color after direct sunlight weakens.
	•	Night: Remove most environmental fill, reduce distant contrast, and use carefully controlled light sources around the train and points of interest.
	•	Dawn: Reveal silhouettes before restoring full ambient illumination, allowing players to recognize the environment before the world fully brightens.
Avoid simply making everything black at night. The threat comes from limited information, not from making navigation impossible.
