For the initial version, I recommend that normal nights remain completely safe around the train, even when optional train equipment is damaged. Use the Pursuit as the primary deliberate exception. This prevents ordinary maintenance failures from unexpectedly undermining the core safety contract.
7.3 Activating Off-Train Threats
Ordinary night enemies should not spawn directly in front of the player or materialize visibly from an empty corridor.
Threat activation pipeline
	1	Detect that the server-authoritative player has crossed the safe-zone boundary.
	2	Check whether the world is in a hostile night phase.
	3	Start an encounter evaluation timer.
	4	Read biome, visibility, player noise, elapsed time outside, and current encounter budget.
	5	Select an eligible enemy archetype.
	6	Choose a hidden spawn point behind appropriate cover.
	7	Verify valid navigation and a viable route to the player.
	8	Spawn the entity outside direct view unless the encounter intentionally includes an emergence animation.
	9	Transition into active pursuit or investigation.
