Encounter pressure
Define a threat score to control intensity:
\[ P = B + N + T + V + A \]
Where:
	•	\(B\) = biome threat contribution.
	•	\(N\) = player noise contribution.
	•	\(T\) = time spent outside the perimeter.
	•	\(V\) = low-visibility contribution.
	•	\(A\) = anomaly or special-event modifier.
The score selects an encounter band, not a deterministic number of enemies. Randomness should choose among equivalent encounters within the selected band.
Noise should make players easier to locate, not automatically summon enemies anywhere in the world.
