8.3 Warning and Preparation
Begin the warning phase approximately 3–5 minutes before the night becomes fully hostile.
Warning indicators:
	•	Radio interference intensifies.
	•	The locomotive produces abnormal vibrations.
	•	Distant metal-on-metal impacts follow the train's movement.
	•	An alarm or warning instrument activates aboard the train.
	•	The sky develops an identifiable anomaly.
	•	A dedicated event indicator tells players how much preparation time remains.
During this phase, the team should be able to:
	•	Load ammunition into mounted weapons.
	•	Repair critical coupling and hull damage.
	•	Top up the locomotive fuel supply.
	•	Move important cargo away from vulnerable exposed areas.
	•	Prepare emergency repair kits.
	•	Assign defensive positions.
Do not spawn the pursuing entity while a major station interaction is unexpectedly interrupting a required tutorial or onboarding sequence.
