8.5 Train Performance During The Pursuit
Define the encounter's pressure from the relationship between the entity's pursuit speed and the locomotive's effective speed.
\[ v_{\text{effective}} = v_{\text{base}} \times M_{\text{load}} \times M_{\text{condition}} \times M_{\text{grade}} \]
Each multiplier represents a controlled, bounded modification. For example:
	•	Excess cargo reduces acceleration.
	•	Poor mechanical condition reduces effective performance.
	•	Steep inclines increase fuel consumption and can reduce speed.
	•	Properly maintained machinery improves consistency.
Use these relationships to drive the chase; avoid teleporting the train or entity to enforce a predetermined result.
