	•	Welding requires line of sight and an appropriate distance.
	•	The player cannot repair a component that has been detached or destroyed beyond its recoverable limit unless a dedicated reconstruction process exists.
	•	Repairing a critical component while the train is moving may involve additional risk.
	•	Severe damage requires more material and more repair time.
	•	The tool's heat or consumable state should prevent infinite repairs.
	•	Other players can assist through power supply, resource delivery, and defensive cover.
